{"name":"High Voltage","hex":"#eeff11","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high voltage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Voltage that is higher than the standard or usual voltage, especially when considered to be dangerous. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to such a voltage; designed to carry or operate at high voltage.","Extremely intense; highly-charged."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_voltage"}],"entries":[{"title":"High voltage","blocks":[{"text":"High voltage is an electrical potential large enough to cause injury or damage. In certain industries, high voltage refers to voltage above a nominal threshold. Equipment and conductors that carry high voltage warrant special safety requirements and procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Plasma-filaments.jpg/330px-Plasma-filaments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_voltage","wikidata":"Q1139740"},{"title":"High Voltage (1976 album)","blocks":[{"text":"High Voltage is the first internationally released album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC. It contains tracks compiled from their first two previous Australia-only issued albums: High Voltage and T.N.T.."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Acdc_high_voltage_international_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Voltage_(1976_album)","wikidata":"Q836320"},{"title":"Voltage","blocks":[{"text":"Voltage, also known as (electrical) potential difference, electric pressure, or electric tension, is the difference in electric potential between two points. In a static electric field, it corresponds to the work needed per unit of charge to move a positive test charge from the first point to the second point. In the International System of Units (SI), the derived unit for voltage is the volt (V)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/AA_AAA_AAAA_A23_battery_comparison-1.jpg/330px-AA_AAA_AAAA_A23_battery_comparison-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voltage","wikidata":"Q25428"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Electrostatic-discharge.jpg/250px-Electrostatic-discharge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Electrostatic-discharge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Electrostatic-discharge.jpg/250px-Electrostatic-discharge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Long-exposure photograph of a Tesla coil showing the repeated electric discharges","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectrostatic-discharge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg/500px-HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg/1280px-HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg/500px-HydroOnePowerTower2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Power lines with high-voltage warning sign","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHydroOnePowerTower2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Kaanaan_polttolaitos_ja_Kemiran_putkia.jpg/500px-Kaanaan_polttolaitos_ja_Kemiran_putkia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u